# Software factory

You are working in a Cursor-native software factory kit.

- Read `factory.config.json` before git writes. Honor `policy.*`. Never push to `main`, `master`, or the default branch.
- Factory work uses `/factory` and `.cursor/skills/factory-pipeline/SKILL.md`. When `chat.autoStart` is true (kit default), a plain-chat **work item** also starts the pipeline; see factory-pipeline **Chat auto-start** and `references/chat-auto-start.md`. Do not auto-start on questions, review-only, or read-only messages. First-time GitHub and workspace setup uses `/factory-setup` and `.cursor/skills/factory-setup/SKILL.md`. Kit upgrades use `/factory-upgrade` and `.cursor/skills/factory-upgrade/SKILL.md`. Do not skip stations. Do not implement in the orchestrator thread. The reviewer must not see the implementer's reasoning, only the plan, branch, and diff. Multi-phase work: one full pipeline and one PR per phase; running all phases in a row is fine, abbreviating any phase is not. Analyst may split a job into child issues after analysis (`github.decomposeIssue`); each child gets the full pipeline. Never merge to the default branch when `policy.merge` is `user`.
- Durable repo facts go in `factory/brain.md`. Jobs go in `factory/queue/`. Handoff documents go in `factory/artifacts/` and travel by id. After each station, rebuild `factory/ui/data.js`.
- Prose for humans follows `.cursor/skills/writing-quality/SKILL.md`.
- UI work uses a design contract. Load `.cursor/skills/frontend-design/` and `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/` from this repo. Do not invent a palette when `design-system/MASTER.md` or a design artifact already exists.
